Own the NSErrors Metal returns, and run pipeline tasks and display queries in autorelease pools.

Metal returns its NSError out-parameters autoreleased, and DXMT keeps each error in a WMT::Reference<WMT::Error>,
which releases it: when a worker thread exits, its implicit pool releases errors that are already freed.
winemetal_unix.c retains each returned error, Metal.hpp takes every NSError out-parameter as a Reference<Error>&
released before the call writes it, and the pipeline tasks (d3d11_pipeline_cache.cpp) and per-Present display
queries (winemetal_unix.c) run in autorelease pools. Applies after wz-n-dxmt-0001. Test: qa/n/pso-reject.sh.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (a change to DXMT).

